    {
      "id": "rnaseq-note-samples",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -260,
        "y": 60
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Samples",
        "icon": "StickyNote",
        "noteText": "The samplesheet lists the sequencing runs: one row per FASTQ file or pair. 'sample' groups runs of the same sample (WT_REP1 has two), 'fastq_2' is empty for single-end reads, and 'strandedness' is auto, forward, unstranded or reverse.\n\nYour own data: replace the rows, or upload the FASTQ files to a File Input node and refer to them by name.",
        "inputs": [],
        "outputs": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rnaseq-note-references",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -260,
        "y": 360
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Reference genome",
        "icon": "StickyNote",
        "noteText": "The genome sequence (--fasta) and its gene annotation (--gtf). The pipeline builds the STAR and Salmon indexes from them.\n\nYour own data: set both to the URL or path of your organism's files (e.g. from Ensembl or GENCODE), or upload them and use the file names.",
        "inputs": [],
        "outputs": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rnaseq-note-pipeline",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 480,
        "y": 440
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Pipeline settings",
        "icon": "StickyNote",
        "noteText": "Double-click the pipeline to see all its parameters. 'Use the pipeline's test profile' is on: it fills in the test data's other settings. Turn it off when you use your own samples and genome.\n\nThe default aligner is STAR with Salmon quantification (--aligner star_salmon).",
        "inputs": [],
        "outputs": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rnaseq-note-resources",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 860,
        "y": 0
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Running it",
        "icon": "StickyNote",
        "noteText": "Needs the Docker install of N-WAVE (the browser demo can only build and export). Its first run downloads several GB of containers.\n\nResources: the run is limited to 4 CPUs and 8 GB of memory (Execution settings > Resources); the test data needs at least 6 GB. Expect 15–30 minutes on a laptop.\n\nExport project gives you a folder with run.sh to run it anywhere with Nextflow and Docker.",
        "inputs": [],
        "outputs": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rnaseq-note-results",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 860,
        "y": 320
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Results",
        "icon": "StickyNote",
        "noteText": "When the run finishes, double-click the pipeline node: its Results section links the reports. Open multiqc_report.html for the summary of every sample (QC, alignment rates, counts).\n\nGene counts are in star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts.tsv.",
        "inputs": [],
        "outputs": []
      }
    }
  ],
